1
00:00:13,350 --> 00:00:14,280
Excuse me, officer.

2
00:00:14,280 --> 00:00:15,340
Can you help me?

3
00:00:15,340 --> 00:00:16,580
Sure.

4
00:00:16,580 --> 00:00:17,500
Can you tell me

5
00:00:17,500 --> 00:00:21,790
how to get to Linden Street, in Riverdale?

6
00:00:21,790 --> 00:00:23,250
Riverdale, New York."

7
00:00:23,250 --> 00:00:25,380
You should take the number 1 subway.

8
00:00:25,380 --> 00:00:26,470
Is there a station near here?

9
00:00:26,470 --> 00:00:28,390
Yes. The station's that way.

10
00:00:28,390 --> 00:00:29,770
You should take the number 1 train

11
00:00:29,770 --> 00:00:31,020
to Van Cortlandt Park.

12
00:00:31,020 --> 00:00:34,180
Number 1 train to Van Cortlandt Park. Thank you.

13
00:00:34,180 --> 00:00:35,300
Anytime. Good luck.

14
00:00:35,300 --> 00:00:38,760
Remember, the number 1 train. The uptown platform.

15
00:00:38,760 --> 00:00:40,980
Thank you.

16
00:00:40,980 --> 00:00:57,290
You're welcome.

17
00:00:57,290 --> 00:00:59,870
Is this pink too bright for me?

18
00:00:59,870 --> 00:01:09,960
Mmm-hmm. It is a very bright pink.

19
00:01:09,960 --> 00:01:14,620
Try this. It's size eight.

20
00:01:14,620 --> 00:01:16,530
But I wear size ten.

21
00:01:16,530 --> 00:01:21,190
How about green? It's size ten.

22
00:01:21,190 --> 00:01:23,910
Let me try it on.

23
00:01:23,910 --> 00:01:29,700
I'm taking too much of your time.

24
00:01:29,700 --> 00:01:30,900
It's six o'clock.

25
00:01:30,900 --> 00:01:32,680
Where's my husband?

26
00:01:32,680 --> 00:01:34,850
I was expecting him here at five forty-five.

27
00:01:34,850 --> 00:01:37,130
Don't worry. The traffic is very heavy at this hour.

28
00:01:37,130 --> 00:01:41,650
I know. But we're going to be late for dinner.

29
00:01:41,650 --> 00:01:43,040
I'll take this green sweater.

30
00:01:43,040 --> 00:01:44,380
I like the color on me, don't you?

31
00:01:44,380 --> 00:01:52,170
I think it looks terrific on you.

32
00:01:52,170 --> 00:01:53,380
I'm sorry I'm so late.

33
00:01:53,380 --> 00:01:56,290
I had a really bad day.

34
00:01:56,290 --> 00:01:58,420
It's ten after six. We're late.

35
00:01:58,420 --> 00:02:00,530
Robbie's cooking tonight, and dinner's at six thirty.

36
00:02:00,530 --> 00:02:03,610
I know. I know. I'm really sorry.

37
00:02:03,610 --> 00:02:05,930
I left my bag of film on the ferry.

38
00:02:05,930 --> 00:02:07,960
I went back for it, but the ferry was gone.

39
00:02:07,960 --> 00:02:10,380
I lost a whole day's work.

40
00:02:10,380 --> 00:02:13,140
I'll call the Staten Island Ferry lost-and-found office.

41
00:02:13,140 --> 00:02:21,330
I didn't think of that. Thanks.

42
00:02:21,330 --> 00:02:22,390
Hello.

43
00:02:22,390 --> 00:02:23,980
Yes. The number, please,

44
00:02:23,980 --> 00:02:29,300
of the Staten Island Ferry lost-and-found office.

45
00:02:29,300 --> 00:02:35,350
Five five five...zero eight zero eight.

46
00:02:35,350 --> 00:02:38,070
Thank you.

47
00:02:38,070 --> 00:02:40,330
I really appreciate it, Marilyn.

48
00:02:40,330 --> 00:02:41,510
Hello.

49
00:02:41,510 --> 00:02:45,380
Did anyone find a camera bag this afternoon,

50
00:02:45,380 --> 00:02:48,860
a small canvas bag,

51
00:02:48,860 --> 00:02:55,630
on the J. F. Kennedy Ferry?...No?

52
00:02:55,630 --> 00:02:57,800
Maybe someone will find it.

53
00:02:57,800 --> 00:03:01,080
The name is Stewart, Richard Stewart.

54
00:03:01,080 --> 00:03:04,500
And the telephone number is five five five...

55
00:03:04,500 --> 00:03:10,910
three oh nine oh. Thank you.

56
00:03:10,910 --> 00:03:13,990
Sorry, Richard. They don't have it.

57
00:03:13,990 --> 00:03:18,470
Thanks, anyway.

58
00:03:18,470 --> 00:03:20,090
There was a girl on the ferry.

59
00:03:20,090 --> 00:03:21,210
Now maybe...

60
00:03:21,210 --> 00:03:24,210
Tell me about it on the way home.
